{{!-- A1, "two-column list", on an author archive: the centred profile over compact rows.

	{{> "author/a1"}}

The author archive shares the Feed's `feed_layout` setting for the same reason the tag archive
does: a buyer picking "a wide row per post" meant it wherever posts are listed.

The row is archive/row.hbs with `tagEyebrow` on — every post here is by the same writer, so the
subject leads and the date signs off, where a tag archive does the reverse. The two sizes are the
design's: a 25px headline and 30px of row padding against the tag archive's 26 and 32.

No lead story on this Surface in either layout. The design draws one on the tag archive and none
here, and a writer's page is a body of work rather than a front page. --}}
{{#author}}
	{{> "author/header" total=../pagination.total}}
{{/author}}

<section
	id="posts"
	aria-label="{{t "Posts"}}"
	style="--container-max:1120px"
	class="border-border container border-t">
	{{#foreach posts}}
		{{> "archive/row" tagEyebrow=true titleClass="text-[25px] leading-[1.2]" padding="py-[30px]"}}
	{{else}}
		<p class="font-body text-muted py-11">{{t "No posts by this writer yet."}}</p>
	{{/foreach}}
</section>
